{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} A [[member]] of the [[Protestant]] Reformed Church of [[France]] during the 16th and 17th [[century]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1980|title=AA Book of British Villages|publisher=Drive Publications Ltd|page=178, about [[Eynsford]]|text=The village was once well known for its paper-milling, founded by '''Huguenot''' immigrants in 1648, which produced high-quality hand-made paper until 1952.}}

